From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: avoid MPC pipe split on the MacBookPro16,1

While the Navi 14 of the MacBookPro16,1 drives the built-in 3072x1920
panel, DML picks two MPC combined pipes for it. With the split the
surface uses an 8 line swath, and the 55 line vblank of the native
timing leaves too few lines for prefetch after the DRAM clock change
wait. DML then reports no DRAM clock change support and DC holds the
UCLK hard minimum at the top level.

The macOS driver sets DalPipeSplitPolicy to 1 on this machine and drives
the panel from one pipe at the native timing. Apply the same policy as
dcdebugmask=0x1 there.

With this change the panel is scanned out by a single HUBP at 3072x1920
with a 4 line swath, the DRAM clock change watermark is 413 us instead
of the dummy latency fallback, and UCLK switches during scanout.

This depends on the UCLK levels matching the VBIOS training, otherwise
UCLK switches during scanout reach a level the SMU cannot switch into.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@
 #include "ivsrcid/ivsrcid_vislands30.h"
 
 #include <linux/backlight.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
@@ -641,7 +642,16 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_init(struct amdgpu_
 		goto error;
 	}
 
-	if (amdgpu_dc_debug_mask & DC_DISABLE_PIPE_SPLIT) {
+	/*
+	 * On the 3072x1920 panel of the MacBookPro16,1 the MPC split leaves
+	 * too few vblank lines for prefetch, so DML reports no DRAM clock
+	 * change support and UCLK stays at its top level. The macOS driver
+	 * sets DalPipeSplitPolicy to 1 on these GPUs and drives the panel
+	 * from one pipe.
+	 */
+	if ((amdgpu_dc_debug_mask & DC_DISABLE_PIPE_SPLIT) ||
+	    (adev->pdev->subsystem_vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE &&
+	     dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "MacBookPro16,1"))) {
 		adev->dm.dc->debug.force_single_disp_pipe_split = false;
 		adev->dm.dc->debug.pipe_split_policy = MPC_SPLIT_AVOID;
 	}
